<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal rejects all bids at three-year bond sale.</title>
<headline>Portugal rejects all bids at three-year bond sale.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's Institute for Public Credit Management (IGCP) rejected all bids at its offer to sell 25 billion escudos of three-year bonds, the Bank of Portugal said.  </p>
<p>Bids totalled 52.93 billion escudos with the minimum yield offered being 5.44 percent and the maximum six percent.</p>
<p>At the last such sale on May 13, the weighted average yield was 5.5013 percent.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
